course: dictionary
lesson: 13706
title: Insoluble: not dissolving, or impossible to solve
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Insoluble means something does not dissolve in a liquid, usually water. When you stir sand into water, the sand stays as tiny grains. «Sand is insoluble in water, so it does not disappear when you stir it.» The opposite word is soluble, which means it can dissolve.
explain: Insoluble also has a second meaning: impossible to solve or answer. «The maths puzzle was insoluble, so nobody could find an answer.» Here the puzzle has no solution. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence: is it about a liquid, or about a problem?
explain: Look at the words around insoluble to find its meaning. Words like water, dissolve, or stir mean science. Words like puzzle, answer, or clues mean a problem. «Salt is soluble, but chalk is insoluble» tells you that the two words are opposites, and that salt disappears in water while chalk does not.
fact: Insoluble means not able to dissolve in a liquid, usually water.
fact: Soluble means able to dissolve. Salt and sugar are soluble in water.
fact: Sand, chalk and oil are insoluble in water.
fact: Insoluble solids can be separated from a liquid by filtering.
fact: Insoluble also means impossible to solve: «an insoluble problem» has no answer.
exercise: «Sand is insoluble in water.» What does insoluble mean here? | *Does not dissolve in water | Floats on top of water | Dissolves very quickly | Turns the water blue
exercise: Salt is soluble, but chalk is insoluble. Which one dissolves in water? | Sand | *Salt | Chalk | Oil
exercise: «The maths puzzle was insoluble, so nobody could find an answer.» What does insoluble mean? | Easy to finish before lunch | Very long | *Impossible to solve | Written in pencil
test: «The scientists separated the sand from the water by filtering, because sand is insoluble.» Why could they separate it this way? | *Sand does not dissolve, so it stays as solid grains the filter can catch | Sand floats away from the filter | Filters turn sand into water | Sand dissolves only when it is hot
test: Ella says insoluble means very wet. Which answer is correct? | Very dry and dusty | Clean and shiny | *Not able to dissolve, or impossible to solve | Very wet and soggy
exam: «The detective called the crime an insoluble mystery, because there were no clues left.» What does insoluble mean? | Easy to solve by teatime | Dissolved in the rain | Written in code | *Impossible to solve
